{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You have seen that from the heavens I spoke with you</b> — He commanded that he say to them: after you have seen with your own eyes that <b>from the heavens I spoke with you</b>, and I am the Master in heaven and earth — do not associate gods of silver and gods of gold with Me, for you have no need for any other help besides Me. The measure of the verse is: you shall not make gods of silver with Me, and you shall not make gods of gold for yourselves. In my opinion, the meaning is: you shall not make gods of silver and gods of gold to be for you as gods alongside Me — \"with Me\" — and you shall not make for yourselves at all. He warned against belief in them, then returned and warned against the making alone, as in \"you shall not set up a carved image or a pillar for yourselves\" (Leviticus 26:1).<br>And by way of truth, the meaning of \"with Me\" (אתי) is like the meaning of \"before Me\" (על פני), and I have already hinted at its explanation (Ramban on Exodus 20:3).<br>Rashi wrote (Rashi on Exodus 20:19): <b>\"For from the heavens I spoke with you\"</b> — and another verse says, \"And HaShem descended upon Mount Sinai\" (Exodus 19:20). A third verse comes to decide between them: \"From the heavens He made you hear His voice to discipline you, and on the earth He showed you His great fire\" (Deuteronomy 4:36) — His glory in the heavens and His fire and His might on the earth. This is the language of the Rav. But it is not accurate. Rather, the resolution of the verses is from the midrash of the Sages (Mekhilta here), and it is true that HaShem is in the heavens and His glory was on Mount Sinai, as it says \"for HaShem was in the fire,\" and it is written, \"And You descended upon Mount Sinai and spoke with them from the heavens\" (Nehemiah 9:13). And all the verses are explained in their own language to anyone who knows, and I have already explained everything above (Exodus 19:20). And Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 20:19) that whoever has a heart will understand the reason in the portion of Ki Tissa (Exodus 33:21). And the words of a wise man's mouth are gracious (Ecclesiastes 10:12)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:12:07.391767919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}